WEBVTT

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:14.450
Huh?

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:18.830
Did that memory return?

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:21.040
You poor thing.

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:25.790
I hate to see you like this, Mademoiselle.

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:59.260
"The Case Study of Vanitas"

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:07.560
Please help, Count Orlok!

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.890
It's Vanitas!

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:11.940
He's going to die!

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:13.520
What?

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:16.440
He has refused to get up
since we returned to Paris.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:18.450
It's been over ten days!

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:20.570
When I ask him what's wrong...

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:22.870
There's a pain in my heart.

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:26.700
...that's all he ever says,
and he won't eat.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:31.000
I don't know what I shall do.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.000
You could just let him die.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:34.710
Not so fast, Manet.

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:38.380
Let's hear him out, at least
until Murr finishes eating.

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:41.180
Amelia is out somewhere,

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:44.300
and Vanitas won't go see a doctor.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:45.600
You're my last hope.

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.140
What a big baby!

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:51.100
I'd rather die than have
someone examine my body.

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:52.350
Vanitas.

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:56.570
Besides, this is no ordinary sickness.

00:02:56.570 --> 00:03:01.910
I've reread my medical books,
but they say nothing of what ails me.

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:05.280
So that's why you had a pile
of books beside your bed.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:10.580
Wait, I know! Jeanne
must've put a curse on me!

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:12.080
The Hellfire Witch?

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:13.830
She cursed you?

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:19.300
These symptoms didn't appear until after
Jeanne sucked my blood in Gévaudan.

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:22.720
My face feels flush,

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:26.930
and my heart feels like it's in
a vise and won't stop racing!

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:27.390
--Wait.

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:27.890
--What?
--Wait.

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:29.600
--What?
--Worst of all,

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:31.850
all I can think about is Jeanne,

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:33.230
no matter what I do!

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:35.190
What in the devil is this?!

00:03:35.190 --> 00:03:38.480
What in the hell is happening to me?!

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:41.150
Something strange
happened when she bit me.

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:44.240
It felt so good, far better than usual!

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:45.490
What?!

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:48.950
She must have done something to me!

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:53.080
Maybe her fangs were poisoned,
or she put a curse on me!

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:57.090
Master Orlok?

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:58.840
Get out!

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:03.180
No, please! Let us in!
At least give me some advice!

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:05.840
Count Orlok!

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:08.350
You leave me no choice
but to kick this door down!

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:11.770
Did you hear what he's
threatening to do out there?!

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:15.060
Don't do anything rash, you barbarians!

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:18.270
Huh? Vanitas?

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:02.110
What is this?

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:04.780
I've never felt this way.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:07.700
What am I supposed to do?

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:09.490
<i>J'taime!</i>

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:12.290
While we were apart,
all I could think about was you,

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:14.960
and I suffered a
terrible pain in my heart.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:16.670
Then it dawned on me.

00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:22.170
This pain I feel is my deep
and abiding love for you!

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:26.340
Vanitas, what in the devil is love?

00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:33.640
No. Make it stop.

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:35.770
This can't be happening.

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:40.060
It makes no sense!

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:42.780
Pardon me.

00:05:44.230 --> 00:05:46.280
Roland?!

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:48.950
Oh, dear Vincent.

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:52.120
Fancy meeting you here!

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:55.500
A friend of yours?

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:57.540
Let me introduce you, Vincent.

00:05:57.540 --> 00:06:00.500
This is my comrade in arms, Olivier.

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:02.040
Olivier?

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:03.880
As in the Obsidian?

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:08.050
Have you been causing
trouble outside of work, too?!

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:09.840
He looks terrified.

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:14.850
No, I simply had a drinking contest
with Vincent, but only once.

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:20.020
Then I pity him. You're like a human
sponge when it comes to liquor.

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:22.480
It seems Roland has done you wrong.

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:25.150
Let me buy you a cup of coffee.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:28.740
That's fine, but he
appears to be in a hurry.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:32.490
I'm curious to hear what
you do in your spare time.

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:35.700
Even if it's a woman on the sly.

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:39.120
What? I don't have a lover,
at least not now.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:40.540
Not now?!

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:42.960
You were dumped again?

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:45.380
That dame threw herself
at you the other day!

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:48.670
If anyone is popular
with the ladies, it's you.

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:53.850
Vincent, women simply adore Olivier.

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:55.890
Well, I <i>am</i> quite handsome.

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:58.020
And modest, too!

00:06:58.020 --> 00:06:59.850
In any event,

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:04.110
I'd like to know ahead of time
if you're up to something.

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:06.400
It will spare me some pain later.

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:09.150
Is that so? I feel bad for you, Olivier.

00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:12.360
<i>You're</i> the source of my woes, Roland!

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:18.370
S-Since you're offering,

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:21.210
I think I <i>will</i> have that cup of coffee.

00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:28.710
And you can pilot a small flying
machine at the mooring tower.

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:32.430
Olivier and I were soaring over
Paris before we came here!

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:36.560
Try it before the exposition
begins and the line gets too long!

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:45.860
It's been over 15 minutes,
but Vanitas has yet to say a word.

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:54.030
Your coffee... It's getting cold.

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:56.030
Go on!

00:07:58.080 --> 00:07:59.620
Do you...

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:00.500
Continue.

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:04.080
What I'm asking is...

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:10.090
So you have a lot of
experience with romance?

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:12.130
Experience? Well...

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:15.800
I don't know about me,
but Olivier is quite experienced.

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:17.300
That I won't deny.

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:20.310
Th-This...

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:23.690
This concerns a friend of mine.

00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:27.520
Huh? Oh, sure! Go on!

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:34.780
Lately, he can't think of anything but a
certain woman, no matter how he tries.

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:40.910
He says there's a pain in his heart,
and he can't sleep night after night.

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:42.540
Really?!

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:45.170
And his love interest? What is she like?

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:49.420
Sh-She is beautiful with skin
of white and an ample bosom.

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:50.840
Not bad.

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:55.380
Why can't he stop thinking about her?
Did something happen?

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:58.680
I don't know the details.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:02.390
At first, he was entertained
by her reactions.

00:09:02.390 --> 00:09:05.390
He thought that was the only attraction.

00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:09.400
But there were so many
sides of her he never expected.

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:12.190
It threw him for a loop.

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:15.990
The other day, she threw him down
as if to claim him, heart and soul,

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:17.610
and then she kissed him!

00:09:17.610 --> 00:09:19.330
And then...!

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:26.460
He saw her smile like
she had never before.

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:28.460
That's about it.

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:34.130
But that was enough to
sear her image into my mind.

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:38.640
Olivier.

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:43.520
Pardon me. My dessert
went down the wrong way.

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:46.940
So it's like she shines.

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:48.100
You know what it is?!

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:52.440
Of course I do, Vincent. Simply put...

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:54.440
...it's love!

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:56.900
What's wrong?

00:09:56.900 --> 00:09:58.410
Love?

00:09:58.410 --> 00:10:02.490
That's what it really is? This is...

00:10:02.490 --> 00:10:04.120
...true love?

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:07.080
How does one cure this disease?

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:10.000
I'm used to pain, but nothing like this!

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:10.540
--Van--

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:11.290
--I can't stand this agony.
--Van--

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:13.590
--I can't stand this agony.

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:18.880
This sickly feeling like I'm being
rewritten from the inside...

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:20.590
I cannot bear it.

00:10:20.590 --> 00:10:24.720
He's not even pretending
this is about his friend anymore.

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:26.930
B-But, dear Vincent,

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:32.860
it sounds like your love interest feels
the same about you from what you've said.

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:36.570
What?

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:37.860
You didn't know?

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:39.990
That can't be true.

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:41.120
No way in hell.

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:42.120
Why not?

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:43.580
Why not?!

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:47.540
Because I approached her,
thinking she'd never love me.

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:49.210
Why?

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:52.880
Because it's revolting!

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:58.590
Why would anyone love someone like me?

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:03.390
I am shocked.

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:08.390
You despise yourself
even more than I'd thought.

00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:10.560
What?!

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:13.730
But it will be all right!
You've nothing to fear!

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:19.530
If you are incapable of loving yourself,
I will double the love I have for you!

00:11:19.530 --> 00:11:22.660
God's love rains down
on all in equal measure!

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:25.160
You have simply failed to notice!

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:28.910
You need not be scared to love someone.

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:31.870
<i>You're</i> scaring me right now!

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:35.790
Never mind! I'm an idiot
for discussing this with you!

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:37.550
Idiot. Idiot!

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:41.510
Don't ever come near me again, you idiot!

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:44.350
Idiot!

00:11:44.350 --> 00:11:46.220
Dear Gilbert?

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:49.180
Go on. You better go after him.

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:53.690
Right. See you later, Roland.

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:59.150
So, he's that Blue Moon Clan
member everyone's talking about.

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:02.030
Oh, the cat's out of the bag?

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:11.620
That's unlike you to
get attached to someone.

00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:14.630
Have I grown attached to him?

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:17.500
That's how it looks to me.

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:23.180
I see. Well, Vanitas always seems
like he's at the end of his rope.

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:28.930
It's as if he'd fall to pieces the
moment I took my eyes off him.

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:31.270
I just can't leave him like that.

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:41.780
I am truly sorry for what has transpired.

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:45.660
I have caused you so much trouble.

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:47.870
You were acting on my lord uncle's orders.

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:51.000
There's no need to worry about it.

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:53.790
Now, let's enjoy our tea
before it gets cold.

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:59.380
And please tell me all you can
about what happened in Gévaudan.

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:05.970
I see. That must have
been terrible, Jeanne.

00:13:05.970 --> 00:13:09.640
I don't know if it's my place to say,

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:14.850
but I'm glad you didn't
have to kill your dear friend.

00:13:14.850 --> 00:13:19.020
After all, I don't want
to see you looking sad.

00:13:19.020 --> 00:13:20.940
Master Luca.

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:29.700
So, where is Chloé d'Apchier now?

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:31.080
I do not know.

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:36.170
I left the rest to Vanitas and
immediately departed from Gévaudan.

00:13:36.170 --> 00:13:37.080
Why?

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:39.670
I knew I might be questioned on my return,

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:43.510
so we decided it was best if
I didn't know Chloé's whereabouts.

00:13:43.510 --> 00:13:45.760
I see.

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:48.970
But I'm sure she'll be fine.

00:13:48.970 --> 00:13:52.430
I now know the sort of person Vanitas is.

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:56.730
He would never mistreat Chloé.

00:13:56.730 --> 00:14:02.400
Y-You have grown to trust him
quite a bit, h-haven't you?

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:05.740
It almost seems unnatural.

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:10.410
Yes, now that you mention it,
it does seem strange.

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:17.080
Ever since I returned from Gévaudan,
I can't get Vanitas out of my mind.

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:20.420
I no longer feel the revulsion I once did.

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:23.630
It's as if there's a shine to him now.

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:27.930
It's strange, but my heart
begins to race when I think of him.

00:14:27.930 --> 00:14:31.100
But that makes no sense!

00:14:31.100 --> 00:14:33.260
I mean, it's as if...

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:38.850
It's as if you've... fallen for Vanitas!

00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:45.860
I've fallen for him?

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:48.150
For Vanitas?

00:14:52.910 --> 00:14:53.910
Oh.

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:55.580
Oh?

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:12.890
Please help, Dominique!

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:15.930
Something is terribly wrong
with my dear Jeanne!

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:17.680
Is something wrong, Jeanne?!

00:15:17.680 --> 00:15:23.520
Yes, Lady Dominique. It seems...

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:27.650
It seems I really have fallen for Vanitas.

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:33.160
Let's slow down and
discuss this rationally.

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:34.780
Of course!

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:38.250
Jeanne, have you eaten
anything unusual lately?

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:40.160
Or perhaps you bumped your head.

00:15:40.160 --> 00:15:43.040
Did someone poison you
when they sucked your blood?!

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:44.790
Or did you injure your eyes?!

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:45.630
What?

00:15:45.630 --> 00:15:49.840
How else are we supposed to believe
you could fall for a man like that?!

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:50.970
That's right!

00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:53.260
I'd understand if you'd fallen for Noé!

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:53.840
--Huh?

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:54.550
--He's strong, handsome,
kind, and adorable!
--Huh?

00:15:54.550 --> 00:15:56.350
--He's strong, handsome,
kind, and adorable!

00:15:56.350 --> 00:15:57.350
Domi!

00:15:57.350 --> 00:16:00.060
Surely anyone would fall for him!

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:01.980
Hard pass on Noé, too!

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:04.190
I don't want that, either!

00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:07.520
Vanitas is like the polar opposite of Noé!

00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:09.780
He treated you horribly, remember?

00:16:09.780 --> 00:16:14.700
But Vanitas saved me so many times.

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:16.950
He's a good person.

00:16:16.950 --> 00:16:21.540
Is it all or nothing when it
comes to this girl's feelings?

00:16:21.540 --> 00:16:23.670
I'm so happy.

00:16:23.670 --> 00:16:24.710
Huh?

00:16:24.710 --> 00:16:30.420
After all, I thought romantic love was
something a bourreau could never have.

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:32.680
It makes one's heart race.

00:16:32.680 --> 00:16:36.390
And it's so thrilling,
one can't sit still.

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:40.720
But something has me a bit concerned.

00:16:40.720 --> 00:16:42.810
Yes, what is it?

00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:46.560
If my feelings for him
continue to grow unabated,

00:16:46.560 --> 00:16:50.400
and I see him again while I'm like this...

00:16:52.110 --> 00:16:54.030
...I fear I will push him down

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:57.450
and consummate our love
the moment our eyes meet.

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:00.450
What's gotten into you?!

00:17:00.450 --> 00:17:04.160
Going all the way the first time
is jumping the gun, isn't it?

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:08.000
It's not a matter of being
too fast or slow! It's simply vulgar!

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:09.290
Really?

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:14.130
My mother kept pushing till she got my
father down and took him for her own.

00:17:14.130 --> 00:17:16.010
She taught you this?!

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:19.140
I-It's not my place to criticize
how you were brought up,

00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:24.230
but a proper courtship should
begin with an exchange of letters.

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:26.270
Is that true, Master Luca?

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:27.940
The sky's so purty.

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:28.810
Master Luca?!

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:32.320
Look! You shocked him so badly,
he detached from reality.

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:32.820
--Master Luca, snap out of it!

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:36.280
--That rainbow looks yummy.
--Master Luca, snap out of it!

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:38.410
Have you forgotten already?

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:43.290
He himself said, "I have zero interest in
the sort of person who would love me."

00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:45.870
It's pointless to love a man like that.

00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:47.460
Really?

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:49.040
I suppose you're right.

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:52.670
I must practice now so I can
interact normally with Vanitas.

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:54.420
No! You've got it all wrong!

00:17:54.420 --> 00:17:56.510
Don't worry, Lady Dominque!

00:17:56.510 --> 00:17:59.850
I won't be so foolish as to
let Vanitas know how I feel.

00:17:59.850 --> 00:18:04.560
I developed quite impressive
acting skills on our previous date!

00:18:06.310 --> 00:18:10.150
A date?! What's that
supposed to mean, Jeanne?!

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:11.110
What?

00:18:11.110 --> 00:18:16.740
I-I'm astonished. To think
Jeanne could be so intense.

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:19.820
I never knew she could smile like that.

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:25.660
When we first met, I thought life
had robbed her of self-confidence.

00:18:25.660 --> 00:18:29.330
I thought I'd have to protect her.

00:18:29.330 --> 00:18:31.790
But there was no need.

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:34.760
I don't know if it's due to Vanitas,

00:18:34.760 --> 00:18:37.800
but she's far more expressive than before.

00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:39.970
I can't take my eyes off of her.

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:46.310
I can see why she'd be on Noé's mind.

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:49.730
She is nothing like me.

00:18:51.560 --> 00:18:53.190
Dominique?

00:18:55.730 --> 00:18:59.240
Noé.

00:18:59.240 --> 00:19:01.160
Noé!

00:19:03.990 --> 00:19:07.370
You'll catch cold if you
stay up there much longer.

00:19:07.370 --> 00:19:08.870
Shut it.

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:14.550
I just remembered what Manet
told me when we visited Count Orlok.

00:19:14.550 --> 00:19:16.090
Not interested.

00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:18.720
Ever since we left for Gévaudan,

00:19:18.720 --> 00:19:22.390
there's been a series of
vampire attacks here in Paris.

00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:25.680
Might it not be the work
of a curse-bearer?

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:27.310
No idea.

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:33.610
Vanitas.

00:19:33.610 --> 00:19:39.280
I'd never met a human who loathed vampires
with all their heart until Gévaudan.

00:19:39.280 --> 00:19:41.360
And I hated him for it.

00:19:41.360 --> 00:19:45.580
I couldn't let him win.
And I don't regret our battle.

00:19:45.580 --> 00:19:49.000
But it got me thinking.

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:54.500
What made you take one path
and Astolfo another?

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:59.630
The Vampire of the Blue Moon
no doubt played a major role.

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:02.010
But before that, the smallest of things,

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:06.220
like the flutter of a butterfly's wings,
could've changed your path.

00:20:10.890 --> 00:20:16.360
And then it might have been you
I fought in Gévaudan.

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:18.690
What's your point?

00:20:22.490 --> 00:20:27.120
I'm glad it wasn't a Chasseur
I met that day on La Baleine,

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:30.950
but rather a doctor
who's a vampire specialist.

00:20:34.290 --> 00:20:39.670
Of course, I still don't like you.

00:20:39.670 --> 00:20:41.590
Nevertheless...

00:20:44.130 --> 00:20:48.430
I'm glad you're here just the way you are.

00:20:48.430 --> 00:20:51.060
I know it all sounds self-serving,

00:20:51.060 --> 00:20:53.810
but I wanted you to know.

00:21:06.530 --> 00:21:09.660
Look, they say it's an amusement park.

00:21:09.660 --> 00:21:14.000
Looks like fun. I hope I can go someday.

00:21:17.210 --> 00:21:21.050
Oh, Mademoiselle. Not again?

00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:31.350
This won't do.

00:21:31.350 --> 00:21:36.270
I asked you to bring Monsieur Noé to me.

00:21:36.270 --> 00:21:39.980
Why won't you do as I say?

00:21:39.980 --> 00:21:43.610
If you won't bring him to me,

00:21:43.610 --> 00:21:47.160
I'll just have to use you as bait.

00:21:55.500 --> 00:21:59.420
Forgive me, Mademoiselle Domi.

00:22:02.760 --> 00:22:05.010
"The Incurable Disease"

00:23:37.100 --> 00:23:41.500
"Scars"
